<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16967" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">exossis</span></b> , e, and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">exossus</span></b> , a, um, adj.
		ex-ŏs, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>without bones</i>, <i>boneless</i>
			(post-class.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cum sit (lepus marinus) cetera exossis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. Mag. p. 300, 13</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense5"><b>(a).</b>
			<i>Pliant</i>, <i>limber</i>, <i>supple</i>, <i>yielding</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">exossis plane et enervis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. Mag. p. 322, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">enervam et exossam saltationem explicat,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Met. 1, p. 104, 3</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense5"><b>(b).</b>
			<i>Loose</i>, <i>negligent</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dictio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sid. Ep. 6, 18</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
</div>